    "body": "Neovim may hang during shutdown after receiving SIGHUP. A queued multi-line Lua error triggers the -- More -- prompt, which waits indefinitely for input from an already closed terminal.\n\nMeanwhile, libuv timers continue running, and vim.schedule() keeps adding events and Lua registry references, causing unbounded memory growth.\n\nIn a real case, the process remained alive for days and consumed approximately 135 GB of memory.\n\nRoot Cause\n\nnlua_schedule() checks main_loop.closing but ignores exiting.\n\nSince main_loop.closing is set only after event_teardown(), new events can still be queued while shutdown is blocked inside do_more_prompt().\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Save `repro.lua` (below) and run `nvim -u repro.lua -i NONE -n --noplugin` in a terminal\n   (the TUI starts an `nvim --embed` server child).\n2. From another terminal, send SIGHUP to the **server** process: `kill -HUP <pid of 'nvim ... --embed'>`.\n3. Do not press any key.\n\n```lua\nvim.o.more = true\nlocal uv = vim.uv\nlocal timer = uv.new_timer()\ntimer:start(0, 4, vim.schedule_wrap(function() end))\nlocal hup = uv.new_signal()\nhup:start(\"sighup\", function()\n  error(\"boom\\n\" .. string.rep(\"line\\n\", 300)) -- multi-line luv callback error\nend)\n```\n### Proposed fix\n\n```diff\n--- a/src/nvim/lua/executor.c\n+++ b/src/nvim/lua/executor.c\n@@ -577,8 +577,9 @@\n   lua_pushnil(lstate);\n   // If main_loop is closing don't schedule tasks to run in the future,\n-  // otherwise any refs allocated here will not be cleaned up.\n-  if (main_loop.closing) {\n+  // otherwise any refs allocated here will not be cleaned up. \"closing\" is only\n+  // set after event_teardown() drained the queue, so also check \"exiting\".\n+  if (main_loop.closing || exiting) {\n     lua_pushliteral(lstate, \"main loop is closing\");\n     return 2;\n   }\n--- a/src/nvim/message.c\n+++ b/src/nvim/message.c\n@@ -2519,7 +2519,7 @@\n         if (p_more && lines_left == 0 && State != MODE_HITRETURN\n-            && !msg_no_more) {\n+            && !msg_no_more && !exiting) {\n           if (do_more_prompt(NUL)) {\n```\n\n",
